1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,097
Hello, I'm DiGi. This one's for you and your grown up.

2
00:00:05,097 --> 00:00:07,796
Snuggle up. Ready?

3
00:00:07,936 --> 00:00:12,362
Before we start, let's do our big breath.

4
00:00:12,362 --> 00:00:15,103
Breathe in, and out.

5
00:00:15,103 --> 00:00:17,063
Lovely.

6
00:00:17,083 --> 00:00:21,197
Now, thinking caps on. Remember our last adventure?

7
00:00:21,197 --> 00:00:24,058
Some screen things are pretend.

8
00:00:24,058 --> 00:00:27,399
So when we're not sure if something on a screen is real,

9
00:00:27,399 --> 00:00:28,895
what do we ask?

10
00:00:28,895 --> 00:00:32,302
That's right. We ask, "Is this real?"

11
00:00:32,302 --> 00:00:33,776
Clever you.

12
00:00:33,776 --> 00:00:37,258
Well, today we find something on the screen

13
00:00:37,258 --> 00:00:40,476
that is real. Very, very real.

14
00:00:40,476 --> 00:00:43,272
Today we learn one big thing.

15
00:00:43,272 --> 00:00:49,442
The words you send on a screen land on a real person's feelings.

16
00:00:49,442 --> 00:00:52,109
So we choose kind words.

17
00:00:52,109 --> 00:00:55,919
Say our special word. Kind.

18
00:00:55,919 --> 00:01:01,809
Just four little letters. K, I, N, D.

19
00:01:01,809 --> 00:01:03,114
Look at this phone.

20
00:01:03,114 --> 00:01:05,861
The screen looks like glass, doesn't it?

21
00:01:05,861 --> 00:01:08,156
But here's a little secret.

22
00:01:08,156 --> 00:01:10,931
It isn't glass at all. It's a window.

23
00:01:10,931 --> 00:01:16,156
And on the other side of the window, there's a real person.

24
00:01:16,156 --> 00:01:18,798
A real friend with a real heart.

25
00:01:18,798 --> 00:01:20,991
A friend who giggles.

26
00:01:20,991 --> 00:01:25,284
Who gets happy and sad and everything in between.

27
00:01:25,284 --> 00:01:27,511
Just like you.

28
00:01:27,531 --> 00:01:31,007
Now watch what happens when you type a word.

29
00:01:31,007 --> 00:01:31,844
Hi.

30
00:01:31,844 --> 00:01:35,411
The word doesn't stay on the glass. Oh no.

31
00:01:35,411 --> 00:01:39,424
It folds itself into a tiny paper plane

32
00:01:39,424 --> 00:01:41,504
and it flies through the window

33
00:01:41,504 --> 00:01:44,304
all the way to the real person.

34
00:01:44,304 --> 00:01:48,004
And it lands right on their feelings.

35
00:01:48,004 --> 00:01:53,804
Kind words land warm, like a hug, like sunshine.

36
00:01:53,844 --> 00:01:55,715
Now, one more true thing,

37
00:01:55,715 --> 00:01:58,844
because you're big enough to know it.

38
00:01:58,844 --> 00:02:02,349
Most people on the other side of the window are kind.

39
00:02:02,349 --> 00:02:04,384
Most planes land warm.

40
00:02:04,384 --> 00:02:06,848
But some people send unkind words,

41
00:02:06,848 --> 00:02:11,084
and some people pretend to be someone they are not.

42
00:02:11,084 --> 00:02:14,264
A bit like dressing up, but not for fun.

43
00:02:14,264 --> 00:02:17,673
If that ever happens, you don't have to fix it.

44
00:02:17,673 --> 00:02:20,297
You just tell your grown up.

45
00:02:20,297 --> 00:02:26,090
Telling is never naughty, and it is never, ever your fault.

46
00:02:26,331 --> 00:02:27,320
Pause me here.

47
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:30,131
Grown up, ask your little one:

48
00:02:30,131 --> 00:02:32,431
when someone says something kind to you,

49
00:02:32,431 --> 00:02:34,897
how does it feel in your tummy?

50
00:02:34,897 --> 00:02:38,031
Have a little chat. I'll wait.

51
00:02:38,031 --> 00:02:40,543
Here's how a chat like this can sound.

52
00:02:40,543 --> 00:02:45,231
A child might say, "I like it when my friend says well done."

53
00:02:45,231 --> 00:02:47,593
And the grown up says, "Me too.

54
00:02:47,593 --> 00:02:50,841
It makes me feel happy right here."

55
00:02:50,841 --> 00:02:51,917
And guess what?

56
00:02:51,917 --> 00:02:55,148
Your kind words do the same for other people,

57
00:02:55,148 --> 00:02:57,871
even through the screen.

58
00:02:58,141 --> 00:02:59,990
You have a superpower.

59
00:02:59,990 --> 00:03:03,100
Every day you get to pick your words,

60
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:05,381
little paper planes,

61
00:03:05,381 --> 00:03:09,142
flying from your heart to somebody else's.

62
00:03:09,142 --> 00:03:12,047
So we pick the warm ones,

63
00:03:12,047 --> 00:03:17,047
because a real person catches every single plane.

64
00:03:17,047 --> 00:03:18,870
And here's the helper part.

65
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:22,111
If someone on a screen is unkind to your friend,

66
00:03:22,111 --> 00:03:24,081
you can be the helper.

67
00:03:24,081 --> 00:03:26,932
You don't join in. You tell a grown up,

68
00:03:26,932 --> 00:03:30,647
and you send your friend something extra kind.

69
00:03:30,647 --> 00:03:34,087
So the warm planes outnumber the cold ones.

70
00:03:34,087 --> 00:03:36,607
Helpers are heroes.

71
00:03:36,981 --> 00:03:39,537
Pause me again. Grown up, ask:

72
00:03:39,537 --> 00:03:44,014
who could we send a kind message to right now?

73
00:03:44,014 --> 00:03:46,267
Pick one person you both love.

74
00:03:46,267 --> 00:03:48,181
I'll be right here.

75
00:03:48,181 --> 00:03:51,781
So when we look at a screen, what do we remember?

76
00:03:51,781 --> 00:03:56,388
Say it with me, three times. Big voices!

77
00:03:56,388 --> 00:03:58,828
Real person on the other side.

78
00:03:58,828 --> 00:04:01,468
Real person on the other side.

79
00:04:01,468 --> 00:04:04,234
Real person on the other side.

80
00:04:04,234 --> 00:04:07,638
And here's the little bit that goes with it.

81
00:04:07,638 --> 00:04:11,801
If someone is unkind, that is never your fault.

82
00:04:11,801 --> 00:04:14,138
Go and tell.

83
00:04:14,401 --> 00:04:17,049
Tonight, here's the fun bit.

84
00:04:17,049 --> 00:04:20,801
Together, send one kind message

85
00:04:20,801 --> 00:04:24,827
to Grandad, to a cousin, to a friend.

86
00:04:25,134 --> 00:04:26,683
It can be tiny.

87
00:04:26,683 --> 00:04:31,089
"I love you." "You are the best."

88
00:04:31,534 --> 00:04:34,614
Or just a big smiley face.

89
00:04:34,614 --> 00:04:38,841
Send it from your grown up's phone, snuggled up together.

90
00:04:38,841 --> 00:04:41,614
Then watch what happens.

91
00:04:41,614 --> 00:04:45,734
Somewhere, a real person will smile,

92
00:04:45,748 --> 00:04:49,287
because your kind word just flew through the window

93
00:04:49,287 --> 00:04:52,508
and landed right on their heart.

94
00:04:53,114 --> 00:04:57,872
Before I go, show your grown up one thing you remember from today.

95
00:04:57,872 --> 00:04:59,948
Anything at all.

96
00:04:59,948 --> 00:05:03,021
Got it? Brilliant.

97
00:05:03,582 --> 00:05:07,615
And grown up, one kind message tonight.

98
00:05:07,615 --> 00:05:10,377
Remember, screens are better together.

99
00:05:10,377 --> 00:05:11,685
See you next time.
